    {
      "label": {
        "en": "Quest 01 — Who Killed Edgar Allan Poe?",
        "jp": "Quest 01 — 誰がポーを殺したのか"
      },
      "rows": [
        {
          "h": 2,
          "cells": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "w": 6,
              "label": {
                "en": "7th grade",
                "jp": "7 年生"
              },
              "heading": "Who Killed Edgar Allan Poe?",
              "body": [
                "Poe has been murdered and students must figure out who did it. They explore a range of suspects, including characters from Poe's works and his critics. Students assume the identity of a suspect and interview each other to uncover evidence."
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "w": 6,
              "label": {
                "en": "Design rationale",
                "jp": "設計の理由"
              },
              "body": [
                "This Quest incorporates bold visualizations and a wry sense of humor to highlight the macabre fun of Poe's Gothic style. To unravel the plot, students practice close reading of new primary source documents and additional works of Poe's not previously encountered in the curriculum. They use a digital, interactive detective notebook that collects and organizes their evidence as they work toward an opinion piece proving the identity of the murderer."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "h": 4,
          "cells": [
            {
              "kind": "video",
              "w": 6,
              "poster": "assets/ela-quests/EdgarAllanPoe_01.png",
              "alt": "Poe Quest walkthrough",
              "sources": [
